## 4) Business Rules (NZ-ready, reliable)

* **Email is required** (frontend + backend). No email → block submission & save (fail fast).
* Invoice numbering: prefix + zero-pad sequence (e.g., `SC-000123`), atomic increment (use `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` or `wpdb->query('LOCK TABLES …')`).
* GST: default 15% NZ; per-line taxable ✓; totals auto-compute; show GST line item visibly.
* Status flow:

  * draft → sent (on email) → viewed (tracking pixel or pay link open) → paid (balance 0) / overdue (past due & balance>0) → void (admin only).
* Deletion: soft delete (retain number/history).
* Validation: numeric fields fixed-point decimals (stringified), never float math; sanitize TinyMCE with `wp_kses_post`.
* Email dispatch:

  * To admin/owner + customer on “Send Invoice”.
  * Block send if any “To” empty.
  * Log every send to `wp_ays_email_log`.
* Files: PDF rendered server-side (DOMPDF or mPDF), stored as transient on demand (don’t bloat uploads).
* Permissions: `manage_ays_invoices` (Owner/Admin), `edit_ays_invoices` (Managers), `view_ays_invoices` (Staff).
* Audit: all changes recorded in `history_json` (or `wp_ays_invoice_events` if you prefer a table).

